soc/tegra: fuse: take the platform from HIDREV when it is available

TEST ONLY (talos-jetson-orin, not part of pkgs#1518). Since 8b8ee2e56f95
("soc/tegra: Use ARM SMCCC to get chip ID, revision, and platform info")
the platform comes from bits [15:8] of the SMCCC SoC revision. TF-A on
Tegra234 puts the HIDREV major revision there (0x401 on Orin NX), so the
kernel reports "Asim QT" and tegra_is_silicon() returns false.

--- a/drivers/soc/tegra/fuse/tegra-apbmisc.c
+++ b/drivers/soc/tegra/fuse/tegra-apbmisc.c
@@ -86,7 +86,12 @@
 #if IS_ENABLED(CONFIG_HAVE_ARM_SMCCC_DISCOVERY)
 	s32 revision = arm_smccc_get_soc_id_revision();
 
-	if (revision >= 0)
+	/*
+	 * TF-A on Tegra194 and Tegra234 reports the HIDREV major revision in
+	 * bits [15:8] of the SoC revision, not the platform. Only use SMCCC
+	 * when HIDREV is not available.
+	 */
+	if (revision >= 0 && !apbmisc_base)
 		return TEGRA_SMCCC_PLATFORM(revision);
 #endif
 	return (tegra_read_chipid() >> 20) & 0xf;
